---
// Reader: a service owner deciding how to adapt a solution and who can help.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../data/contact';
---
<Base title="Implement and adapt a public service | Registry Stack" description="Work with our team to configure and test a public service. Use AI-assisted implementation and review the proposed changes before deployment.">
  <SiteHeader current="customization" />
  <main>
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="customize-title"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI-assisted implementation</p>
      <h1 id="customize-title">Build and adapt a service around your rules.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Bring a service brief or the forms and procedures you already use. Our team uses AI and reusable software to help prepare changes to records, forms and review steps. Your team reviews and tests the result.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref('customization')} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#how-customization-works">See the process</a></div>
      <p class="hero-note">Available through a scoped implementation pilot. Your institution approves the rules, and the service can run without an AI model.</p>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="section" id="how-customization-works" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">From a brief to a service</p><h2 id="process-title">Agree what to change and how to test it.</h2><p>We start with the service you describe, identify a suitable starting point and agree the adaptations with your team.</p></div>
      <ol class="delivery-steps">
        <li><h3>Agree the brief</h3><p>Bring the proposed steps, open questions and scenarios to test. Share any prototype your team has tried with applicants and staff. Your institution resolves open policy questions.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Prepare the changes</h3><p>We use AI to help draft changes to the configuration and application code. Your team can review the proposed screens, permissions and steps alongside the brief.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Test the service together</h3><p>Try a representative application and an exception. Check who can see the request, record a decision and make the resulting change.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Agree the handover</h3><p>Specify the configuration, test cases and operating instructions your team will receive. Name who will run the service and maintain each integration.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="section-note">Still defining the service? <a href="/ai/service-design/">See how to prepare a service brief</a>. You can also <a href="/starters/">browse starting configurations</a> for evaluation.</p>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><h3>Start with public forms and fictional examples</h3><p>These are enough for an initial discussion. Include any restrictions on AI tools or data use in your inquiry so we can assess an appropriate approach before you share confidential material or personal records.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="change-example" aria-labelledby="change-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Illustrative change</p>
        <h2 id="change-title">What changes when children can start school a year earlier?</h2>
        <p>In this example, an education authority opens pre-primary enrolment to children aged five. An assistant could help draft the changes. The delivery team would check all four places against the approved policy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-grid change-grid">
        <article><h3>Eligibility rule</h3><p>Use the approved cut-off date. Test a child who turns five by the cut-off and one who turns five just after it.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Evidence check</h3><p>If the service verifies age with another authority, agree the updated question and test what happens when an answer is unavailable.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Assignment notice</h3><p>Check that the letter tells parents the right programme and start date.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Published guidance</h3><p>Check that the portal and school office give parents the same entry age and date.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="section-note">The education authority reviews the proposed changes and test results before approving the release.</p>
      <div class="editorial-callout">
        <h3>See how one released component is configured and tested</h3>
        <p>A separate Evidence Gateway example uses a fictional licence register. One matching active licence returns a signed status. Two matches or an unavailable source return an error without a status. You can inspect the configuration and run the cases with synthetic data.</p>
        <a class="inline-cta" href="https://github.com/registrystack/registry-stack/tree/v0.46.0/products/evidence/examples/standalone/">Read the licence status example and run instructions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section" id="studio" aria-labelledby="studio-title"><div class="section-inner approach-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Registry Studio · In development</p><h2 id="studio-title">Review suggested changes in Registry Studio.</h2><p>We are building a way to start from your documents, review suggested requirements and see which questions still need your team’s decision. A direct assistant for proposing changes is planned.</p><p>For AI-assisted implementation today, work with our team through a scoped pilot.</p></div>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><h3>Tell us what takes effort to change</h3><p>Show us a form that needs adapting, a review step that keeps changing, or a set of related registers your team maintains.</p><a class="inline-cta" href={describeServiceHref('Registry Studio')} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your customization needs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title"><div class="section-inner"><p class="eyebrow">Implementation and support</p><h2 id="next-title">Define one service to work on together.</h2><p>Agree the outcome, responsibilities and fee before implementation begins.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/pricing/">View implementation options</a></div></section>
  </main><SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .change-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .change-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
